-- title:
--   Théorème 1 (= Lemme 2) — every weak cluster point of the regularized iterates solves the variational inequality (1)
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a real Hilbert space with dual $H'$, let $C\subseteq H$ be convex, closed and bounded, and let $T:H\to H'$ be monotone and hemicontinuous on $C$. Let $(x^n)_{n\ge0}$ be generated by the regularization algorithm: $x^0\in C$ and, for each $n$, $x^{n+1}\in C$ satisfies
--   $$
--   (Tx^{n+1},\, x-x^{n+1})+\langle x^{n+1}-x^n,\, x-x^{n+1}\rangle\ge 0\qquad\forall x\in C .
--   $$
--   Then every weak cluster point $\tilde x$ of $(x^n)$ is a solution of the variational inequality (1):
--   $$
--   \tilde x\in C\quad\text{and}\quad (T\tilde x,\, x-\tilde x)\ge 0\qquad\forall x\in C .
--   $$
--
--   This is the main result of Martinet's note: the first convergence theorem for what is now called the proximal point algorithm. Since $C$ is bounded, weak cluster points exist, so the theorem guarantees that the iteration approaches the solution set.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $H$ is real (`InnerProductSpace ℝ H`, `CompleteSpace H`), $H'$ is `StrongDual ℝ H` and $(\varphi,y)$ is `φ y`. Hemicontinuity is weak-* continuity of $t\mapsto T((1-t)x+ty)$ on $[0,1]$ for $x,y\in C$. The sequence is any sequence satisfying (2) at every step (`IsRegSeq`, which includes $x^0\in C$). A weak cluster point is `MapClusterPt` in `WeakSpace ℝ H`. No hypothesis that (1) has a solution and no boundedness of $T$ is assumed. Lemme 2 of the paper (p. 156) is the same statement, since $M$ is the solution set of (1).
-- source:
--   Martinet, Régularisation d'inéquations variationnelles par approximations successives, R.I.R.O. 4(R-3) (1970), p. 155, Théorème 1 (= Lemme 2, p. 156)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MartinetReg_VI_Setting

namespace MartinetReg.VI

open Filter Topology

/-- Théorème 1, p. 155 (= Lemme 2, p. 156): every weak cluster point of the
regularized iterates `{xⁿ}` is a solution of the variational inequality (1). -/
theorem theorem1 {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (T : H → StrongDual ℝ H) (C : Set H) (hS : Standing T C)
    (x : ℕ → H) (hx : IsRegSeq T C x) :
    ∀ xt : H, IsWeakClusterPt xt x → xt ∈ solSet T C := by sorry

end MartinetReg.VI
